In the 2026-07-28 revision of the Model Context Protocol specification, the JSON-RPC error code for `UnsupportedProtocolVersion` was renumbered to **-32022**.

This is explicitly stated in the `mcp-2026-07-28-changelog.md` file, where it says:
> "Renumber the error codes introduced in this draft accordingly — `HeaderMismatch` `-32001` → `-32020`, `MissingRequiredClientCapability` `-32003` → `-32021`, `UnsupportedProtocolVersion` `-32004` → `-32022` — and add `HeaderMismatchError` to the schema..."

Additionally, the `mcp-2026-07-28-versioning.md` file confirms this error code in its example response:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": -32022,
    "message": "Unsupported protocol version",
    "data": {
      "supported": ["2026-07-28", "2025-11-25"],
      "requested": "1900-01-01"
    }
  }
}
```
